ortably. Norvane, with 2027 capex up 12%, looks financeable through debt.\n- **Equity is the weak spot.** Two utility share offerings were cut back in size. Pellham Power, the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after demand fell short. Pellham's 2027 capex is planned up 18%.\n- **Pellham is cutting spending, not switching to debt.** It said it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves. That suggests debt alone isn't covering its plan, likely because of balance-sheet or rating limits. The documents don't say this directly.\n- **Gaps.** I found no data on leverage, ratings headroom, maturity walls or the total size of 2027 funding needs. I can't say how much debt Pellham could add.\n\nNet: debt markets can fund much of the plans for utilities like Norvane. The plans are not fully financeable for Pellham, so expect its equipment orders to fall below plan. That is a risk to grid equipment demand.\n\nSources are the docs utility-capex-2027, utility-credit and pellham-offering.","ttft_ms":2807,"type":"result","duration_ms":21969,"uuid":"8451f8a1-aa71-4ec5-b830-dbaab19e808d","ttft_stream_ms":1358,"time_to_request_ms":62,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":3,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":5,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":11,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":65,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":206,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":132,"process_rss_mib_result":205,"process_anon_mib_result":123,"p